|         Parameters\n481 |         ----------\n482 |         X : {array-like, sparse matrix} of shape (n_samples, n_features)\n483 |             Document word matrix.\n484 | \n485 |         total_samples : int\n486 |             Total number of documents. It is only used when\n487 |             batch_update is `False`.\n488 | \n489 |         batch_update : bool\n490 |             Parameter that controls updating method.\n491 |             `True` for batch learning, `False` for online learning.\n492 | \n493 |         parallel : joblib.Parallel, default=None\n494 |             Pre-initialized instance of joblib.Parallel\n495 | \n496 |         Returns\n497 |         -------\n498 |         doc_topic_distr : ndarray of shape (n_samples, n_components)\n499 |             Unnormalized document topic distribution.\n500 |         \"\"\"\n501 | \n502 |         # E-step\n503 |         _, suff_stats = self._e_step(\n504 |             X, cal_sstats=True, random_init=True, parallel=parallel\n505 |         )\n506 | \n507 |         # M-step\n508 |         if batch_update:\n509 |             self.components_ = self.topic_word_prior_ + suff_stats\n510 |         else:\n511 |             # online update\n512 |             # In the literature, the weight is `rho`\n513 |             weight = np.power(\n514 |                 self.learning_offset + self.n_batch_iter_, -self.learning_decay\n515 |             )\n516 |             doc_ratio = float(total_samples) / X.shape[0]\n517 |             self.components_ *= 1 - weight\n518 |             self.components_ += weight * (\n519 |                 self.topic_word_prior_ + doc_ratio * suff_stats\n520 |             )\n521 | \n522 |         # update `component_` related variables\n523 |         self.exp_dirichlet_component_ = np.exp(\n524 |             _dirichlet_expectation_2d(self.components_)\n525 |         )\n526 |         self.n_batch_iter_ += 1\n527 |         return\n```\n\nFound function `sklearn/decomposition/_dict_learning.py:_update_dic