 \n469 |     for k in range(n_components):\n470 |         if A[k, k] > 1e-6:\n471 |             # 1e-6 is arbitrary but consistent with the spams implementation\n472 |             dictionary[k] += (B[:, k] - A[k] @ dictionary) / A[k, k]\n473 |         else:\n474 |             # kth atom is almost never used -> sample a new one from the data\n475 |             newd = Y[random_state.choice(n_samples)]\n476 | \n477 |             # add small noise to avoid making the sparse coding ill conditioned\n478 |             noise_level = 0.01 * (newd.std() or 1)  # avoid 0 std\n479 |             noise = random_state.normal(0, noise_level, size=len(newd))\n480 | \n481 |             dictionary[k] = newd + noise\n482 |             code[:, k] = 0\n483 |             n_unused += 1\n484 | \n485 |         if positive:\n486 |             np.clip(dictionary[k], 0, None, out=dictionary[k])\n487 | \n488 |         # Projection on the constraint set ||V_k|| <= 1\n489 |         dictionary[k] /= max(linalg.norm(dictionary[k]), 1)\n490 | \n491 |     if verbose and n_unused > 0:\n492 |         print(f\"{n_unused} unused atoms resampled.\")\n```\n\n\n\n##Searching for term \"partial_fit\"...\n### Search Result:\nFound function `sklearn/multiclass.py:OneVsRestClassifier.partial_fit`.\nFound function `sklearn/multiclass.py:OneVsOneClassifier.partial_fit`.\nFound function `sklearn/multioutput.py:_MultiOutputEstimator.partial_fit`.\nFound function `sklearn/multioutput.py:MultiOutputRegressor.partial_fit`.\nFound function `sklearn/naive_bayes.py:GaussianNB.partial_fit`.\nFound function `sklearn/naive_bayes.py:_BaseDiscreteNB.partial_fit`.\nFound function `sklearn/naive_bayes.py:CategoricalNB.partial_fit`.\nFound function `sklearn/cluster/_kmeans.py:MiniBatchKMeans.partial_fit`.\nFound function `sklearn/cluster/_birch.py:Birch.partial_fit`.\nFound function `sklearn/feature_extraction/text.py:HashingVectorizer.partial_fit`.\nFound function `sklearn/linear_model/_passive_aggressive.py:PassiveAggressiveCla