\n### Search Result:\nInvalid name. \nHint: Valid entity name should be formatted as \"file_path:QualifiedName\" or just \"file_path\".\n\n##Searching for entity `sklearn/utils/_tags.py:get_tags`...\n### Search Result:\nFound function `sklearn/utils/_tags.py:get_tags`.\nSource: Exact match found for entity name `sklearn/utils/_tags.py:get_tags`.\n```\n293 | def get_tags(estimator) -> Tags:\n294 |     \"\"\"Get estimator tags.\n295 | \n296 |     :class:`~sklearn.BaseEstimator` provides the estimator tags machinery.\n297 |     However, if an estimator does not inherit from this base class, we should\n298 |     fall-back to the default tags.\n299 | \n300 |     For scikit-learn built-in estimators, we should still rely on\n301 |     `self.__sklearn_tags__()`. `get_tags(est)` should be used when we\n302 |     are not sure where `est` comes from: typically\n303 |     `get_tags(self.estimator)` where `self` is a meta-estimator, or in\n304 |     the common checks.\n305 | \n306 |     .. versionadded:: 1.6\n307 | \n308 |     Parameters\n309 |     ----------\n310 |     estimator : estimator object\n311 |         The estimator from which to get the tag.\n312 | \n313 |     Returns\n314 |     -------\n315 |     tags : :class:`~.sklearn.utils.Tags`\n316 |         The estimator tags.\n317 |     \"\"\"\n318 | \n319 |     if hasattr(estimator, \"__sklearn_tags__\"):\n320 |         tags = estimator.__sklearn_tags__()\n321 |     else:\n322 |         warnings.warn(\n323 |             f\"Estimator {estimator} has no __sklearn_tags__ attribute, which is \"\n324 |             \"defined in `sklearn.base.BaseEstimator`. This will raise an error in \"\n325 |             \"scikit-learn 1.8. Please define the __sklearn_tags__ method, or inherit \"\n326 |             \"from `sklearn.base.BaseEstimator` and other appropriate mixins such as \"\n327 |             \"`sklearn.base.TransformerMixin`, `sklearn.base.ClassifierMixin`, \"\n328 |             \"`sklearn.base.RegressorMixin`, and `sklearn.base.ClusterMixin`, and \"\n329 |             \"`sklearn.base.OutlierMixin`.\",\n330 |             category=FutureWarning,\n331 |         )\n332 |         tags = default_tags(estimator)\n333 | \n334 |     return tags\n```\n"}, {"content": "Let me analyze the issue and prepare the localization result.\n\nBased on the analysis of the issue and code exploration, here are the key locations that need to be modified to implement the old<->new/new<->old tags conversion system:\n\n```\nsklearn/utils/_tags.py\nline: 457-515\nfunction: _to_new_tags\n# This is where new tags need to be converted to old tags\n\nsklearn/utils/_tags.py\nline: 519-583\nfunction: _to_old_tags\n# Where old tags are converted to new tags\n\nsklearn/utils/estimator_checks.py\nline: 4447-4466\nfunction: check_estimator_tags_renamed\n# Validates the tag system migration\n\nsklearn/utils/validation.py\nline: 2909\nfunction: validate_data\n# Uses get_tags() and needs updating for tag conversion logic\n\nsklearn/base.py\nline: 392-399\nclass: BaseEstimator\nfunction: __sklearn_tags__\n# Default implementation of tags that needs to be considered during conversion\n```\n\nThe issue requires implementing the following features:\n1. Conversion of new tags to old tags (_to_old_tags)\n2. Conversion of old tags to new tags (_to_new_tags)\n3. Support for mixed implementations (both _get_tags/_more_tags vs __sklearn_tags__)\n4. Proper warning handling for estimators without proper tag implementation\n5. Delegation of tag handling to BaseEstimator when appropriate\n\nThe core changes will be in sklearn/utils/_tags.py where the conversion logic is implemented, with supporting modifications in other key files that interact with the tag system.", "role": "assistant", "tool_calls": null, "function_call": null}, {"role": "user", "content": "Verify if the found locations contain all the necessary information to address the issue, and check for any relevant references in other parts of the codebase that may not have appeared in the search results. If not, continue searching for additional locations related to the issue.\nVerify that you have carefully analyzed the impact of the found locations on the repository, especially their dependencies. If you think you have solved the task, rewrite your final answer into the required location-only format, output ONLY the location block, and then call `finish` to finish.\nIMPORTANT: YOU SHOULD NEVER ASK FOR HUMAN HELP.\nDaLIC raw evidence tools remain available throughout the investigation.\nIf your current evidence is either too broad, too few or incomplete, call `get_trace_artifacts` again with more precise filters before finishing.\n"}, {"content": "Let me verify the completeness of the findings by checking additional dependencies and references.\n\nFirst, let's look for any files that reference the tag system:\n\n<function=search_code_snippets>\n<parameter=search_terms>['_get_tags', '_more_tags', '__init__.py']</parameter>\n", "role": "assistant", "tool_calls": null, "function_call": null}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "toolu_01", "name": "search_code_snippets", "content": "OBSERVATION:\nsklearn/utils/estimator_checks.py:check_estimator_tags_renamed\nsklearn/utils/validation.py:validate_data\nsklearn/datasets/__init__.py:__getattr__\nsklearn/datasets/_arff_parser.py:_sparse_data_to_array\nsklearn/cross_decomposition/_pls.py:PLSSVD.fit_transform\nsklearn/datasets/_arff_parser.py:_liac_arff_parser\nsklearn/utils/estimator_checks.py:check_estimator_tags_renamed\nsklearn/utils/validation.py:validate_data\nsklearn/datasets/__init__.py:__getattr__\nsklearn/datasets/_arff_parser.py:_sparse_data_to_array\nsklearn/cross_decomposition/_pls.py:PLSSVD.fit_transform\nsklearn/datasets/_arff_parser.py:_liac_arff_parser\nsklearn/utils/estimator_checks.py:check_estimator_tags_renamed\nsklearn/utils/validation.py:validate_data\nsklearn/datasets/__init__.py:__getattr__\nsklearn/datasets/_arff_parser.py:_sparse_data_to_array\nsklearn/cross_decomposition/_pls.py:PLSSVD.fit_transform\nsklearn/datasets/_arff_parser.py:_liac_arff_parser\n##Searching for term \"_get_tags\"...\n### Search Result:\nFound code snippet in file `sklearn/datasets/__init__.py`.\nSource: Retrieved code content using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n  1 | \"\"\"Utilities to load popular datasets and artificial data generators.\"\"\"\n  2 | \n  3 | # Authors: The scikit-learn developers\n  4 | # SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause\n  5 | \n  6 | import textwrap\n  7 | \n  8 | from ._base import (\n  9 |     clear_data_home,\n 10 |     fetch_file,\n 11 |     get_data_home,\n 12 |     load_breast_cancer,\n 13 |     load_diabetes,\n 14 |     load_digits,\n 15 |     load_files,\n 16 |     load_iris,\n 17 |     load_linnerud,\n 18 |     load_sample_image,\n 19 |     load_sample_images,\n 20 |     load_wine,\n 21 | )\n 22 | from ._california_housing import fetch_california_housing\n 23 | from ._covtype import fetch_covtype\n 24 | from ._kddcup99 import fetch_kddcup99\n 25 | from ._lfw import fetch_lfw_pairs, fetch_lfw_people\n 26 | from ._olivetti_faces import fetch_olivetti_faces\n 27 | from ._openml import fetch_openml\n 28 | from ._rcv1 import fetch_rcv1\n 29 | from ._samples_generator import (\n 30 |     make_biclusters,\n 31 |     make_blobs,\n 32 |     make_checkerboard,\n 33 |     make_circles,\n 34 |     make_classification,\n 35 |     make_friedman1,\n 36 |     make_friedman2,\n 37 |     make_friedman3,\n 38 |     make_gaussian_quantiles,\n 39 |     make_hastie_10_2,\n 40 |     make_low_rank_matrix,\n 41 |     make_moons,\n 42 |     make_multilabel_classification,\n 43 |     make_regression,\n 44 |     make_s_curve,\n 45 |     make_sparse_coded_signal,\n 46 |     make_sparse_spd_matrix,\n 47 |     make_sparse_uncorrelated,\n 48 |     make_spd_matrix,\n 49 |     make_swiss_roll,\n 50 | )\n 51 | from ._species_distributions import fetch_species_distributions\n 52 | from ._svmlight_format_io import (\n 53 |     dump_svmlight_file,\n 54 |     load_svmlight_file,\n 55 |     load_svmlight_files,\n 56 | )\n 57 | from ._twenty_newsgroups import fetch_20newsgroups, fetch_20newsgroups_vectorized\n```\n\nFound code snippet in file `sklearn/datasets/__init__.py`.\nSource: Retrieved code content using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n 59 | __all__ = [\n 60 |     \"clear_data_home\",\n 61 |     \"dump_svmlight_file\",\n 62 |     \"fetch_20newsgroups\",\n 63 |     \"fetch_20newsgroups_vectorized\",\n 64 |     \"fetch_file\",\n 65 |     \"fetch_lfw_pairs\",\n 66 |     \"fetch_lfw_people\",\n 67 |     \"fetch_olivetti_faces\",\n 68 |     \"fetch_species_distributions\",\n 69 |     \"fetch_california_housing\",\n 70 |     \"fetch_covtype\",\n 71 |     \"fetch_rcv1\",\n 72 |     \"fetch_kddcup99\",\n 73 |     \"fetch_openml\",\n 74 |     \"get_data_home\",\n 75 |     \"load_diabetes\",\n 76 |     \"load_digits\",\n 77 |     \"load_files\",\n 78 |     \"load_iris\",\n 79 |     \"load_breast_cancer\",\n 80 |     \"load_linnerud\",\n 81 |     \"load_sample_image\",\n 82 |     \"load_sample_images\",\n 83 |     \"load_svmlight_file\",\n 84 |     \"load_svmlight_files\",\n 85 |     \"load_wine\",\n 86 |     \"make_biclusters\",\n 87 |     \"make_blobs\",\n 88 |     \"make_circles\",\n 89 |     \"make_classification\",\n 90 |     \"make_checkerboard\",\n 91 |     \"make_friedman1\",\n 92 |     \"make_friedman2\",\n 93 |     \"make_friedman3\",\n 94 |     \"make_gaussian_quantiles\",\n 95 |     \"make_hastie_10_2\",\n 96 |     \"make_low_rank_matrix\",\n 97 |     \"make_moons\",\n 98 |     \"make_multilabel_classification\",\n 99 |     \"make_regression\",\n100 |     \"make_s_curve\",\n101 |     \"make_sparse_coded_signal\",\n102 |     \"make_sparse_spd_matrix\",\n103 |     \"make_sparse_uncorrelated\",\n104 |     \"make_spd_matrix\",\n105 |     \"make_swiss_roll\",\n106 | ]\n```\n\n\n\n##Searching for term \"_get_tags\", \"_get_tags _more_tags\"...\n### Search Result:\nFound function `sklearn/utils/_tags.py:get_tags`.\nSource: Retrieved entity using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n293 | def get_tags(estimator) -> Tags:\n294 |     \"\"\"Get estimator tags.\n295 | \n296 |     :class:`~sklearn.BaseEstimator` provides the estimator tags machinery.\n297 |     However, if an estimator does not inherit from this base class, we should\n298 |     fall-back to the default tags.\n299 | \n300 |     For scikit-learn built-in estimators, we should still rely on\n301 |     `self.__sklearn_tags__()`. `get_tags(est)` should be used when we\n302 |     are not sure where `est` comes from: typically\n303 |     `get_tags(self.estimator)` where `self` is a meta-estimator, or in\n304 |     the common checks.\n305 | \n306 |     .. versionadded:: 1.6\n307 | \n308 |     Parameters\n309 |     ----------\n310 |     estimator : estimator object\n311 |         The estimator from which to get the tag.\n312 | \n313 |     Returns\n314 |     -------\n315 |     tags : :class:`~.sklearn.utils.Tags`\n316 |         The estimator tags.\n317 |     \"\"\"\n318 | \n319 |     if hasattr(estimator, \"__sklearn_tags__\"):\n320 |         tags = estimator.__sklearn_tags__()\n321 |     else:\n322 |         warnings.warn(\n323 |             f\"Estimator {estimator} has no __sklearn_tags__ attribute, which is \"\n324 |             \"defined in `sklearn.base.BaseEstimator`. This will raise an error in \"\n325 |             \"scikit-learn 1.8. Please define the __sklearn_tags__ method, or inherit \"\n326 |             \"from `sklearn.base.BaseEstimator` and other appropriate mixins such as \"\n327 |             \"`sklearn.base.TransformerMixin`, `sklearn.base.ClassifierMixin`, \"\n328 |             \"`sklearn.base.RegressorMixin`, and `sklearn.base.ClusterMixin`, and \"\n329 |             \"`sklearn.base.OutlierMixin`.\",\n330 |             category=FutureWarning,\n331 |         )\n332 |         tags = default_tags(estimator)\n333 | \n334 |     return tags\n```\n\n\n\n##Searching for term \"_get_tags\", \"_more_tags\"...\n### Search Result:\nFound funct